{
  "_doc": "ONE list of launch cases read by BOTH suites (tests/js/launcher.test.mjs and tests/test_launcher_api.py), so the sheet's command preview and the server's argv cannot drift apart without a test failing. v = the form values the sheet holds; ctx = commandPreview's context; body = the exact POST body the sheet sends for v (launcherPayload(v) must equal it); tokens = the command's tokens: the preview's first line must split into exactly these, and the route's cmd must split into exactly these once its random parts are masked (the id after --session-id becomes <uuid>, the six hex after the worktree name become xxxxxx). Codex cases run on the conftest fake 0.145 (--no-alt-screen, no --no-daemon, no --approve-for-me) unless a case names `codex_help`: then the fake's --help is that fixture (codex_help_0160.txt has --no-daemon, --approve-for-me and `codex fork`, like the box's 0.161.0) and the case's ctx.caps must equal what GET /api/agents answers for that binary (the sheet's capabilities), so the preview's --no-daemon (box check #92: every Codex preview missed it) cannot drift from the route's line.",
